title: If you want the work off this laptop, rent a Hetzner CPX32 (4 vCPU, 8 GB, about $34 a month) for a month's trial; no machine will make missions faster, since they wait on Claude's thinking, not on the tests.
pid: 71fea003-732f-4c14-ac71-b98bc05de105
body: |2-
  To decide: the first three notes below, each answerable by a line
  typed under it. The rest is the reasons.
  Measured 2026-11-15 on this laptop, with four of its 3.5 GHz
  efficiency cores standing in for a rented machine's four vCPUs.
  Nothing ran on a rented machine, so speeds there are an estimate,
  likely somewhat slower. Prices in euros are converted at the European
  Central Bank's rate of 13 November, $1.105 to the euro.
  The biggest load is building the test programs in debug mode (3.7 GB
  of memory with four built at once), beside the servers and Claude's
  own programs (about 4 GB together). The whole test suite uses less
  than one core: it is mostly waiting. And in the last five days
  Claude's own thinking time was three quarters of all working time,
  the tests 8%.
